      "full_cot": ", I can compute it step by step: r}.\n\nWait, perhaps I should compute it more accurately. Let me compute \\( (1.005)^{12} \\) step by step. I can compute it manually:\n\nFirst, 1.005^2 = 1.010025\n\nThen, 1.010025^2 = approx 1.020150\n\nWait, that's squaring twice. Wait, maybe a better approach is to compute each power step by step:\n\n1.005^1 = 1.005\n\n1.005^2 = 1.005 * 1.005 = 1.010025\n\n1.005^3 = 1.010025 * 1.005 \u2248 1.015075125\n\n1.005^4 \u2248 1.015075125 * 1.005 \u2248 1.020150125\n\n1.005^5 \u2248 1.020150125 * 1.005 \u2248 1.025251253\n\n1.005^6 \u2248 1.025251253 * 1.005 \u2248 1.030376253\n\n1.005^7 \u2248 1.030376253 * 1.005 \u2248 1.035545253\n\n1.005^8 \u2248 1.035545253 * 1.005 \u2248 1.040737253\n\n1.005^9 \u2248 1.040737253 * 1.005 \u2248 1.046026253\n\n1.005^10 \u2248 1.046026253 * 1.005 \u2248 1.051127253\n\n1.005^11 \u2248 1.051127253 * 1.005 \u2248 1.056276253\n\n1.005^12 \u2248 1.056276253 * 1.005 \u2248 1.061585253\n\nSo, approximating, \\( (1.005)^{12} \u2248 1.061585 \\). Therefore, \\( 1 + r \u2248 1.061585 \\), so \\( r \u2248 0.061585 \\), which is 6.1585%. Rounded to the nearest hundredth is 6.16%. So, the equivalent annual rate is approximately 6.16%.\n\nLet me verify that with another method just to be sure. Using the formula for the effective annual rate (EAR):\n\nEAR = (1 + nominal rate / number of compounding periods per year)^number of compounding periods - 1\n\nSo, plugging in the numbers:\n\nEAR = (1 + 0.06 / 12)^12 - 1 \u2248 1.061585 - 1 \u2248 0.061585, which is 6.1585%, same as before. So, rounded to two decimal places is 6.16%.\n\nThus, the equivalent annual interest rate is 6.16%.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.16}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) that would give the same return as a 6 percent annual interest rate compounded monthly, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR). \n\nThe compound interest formula for one year is:\n\\[ A = P \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n \\]\n\nFor monthly compounding, the nominal rate is 6%, compounded monthly, so:\n\\[ A_{\\text{monthly}} = P \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} \\]\n\nFor annual compounding, the amount after one year is:\n\\[ A_{\\text{annual}} = P (1 + r) \\]\n\nSetting these equal, we get:\n\\[ P \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = P (1 + r) \\]\n\nThe principal \\( P \\) cancels out, leaving:\n\\[ \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nCalculating the inside of the left side:\n\\[ 1 + \\frac{0.06}{12} = 1 + 0.005 = 1.005 \\]\n\nSo, the equation becomes:\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nUsing step-by-step calculation:\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.061585 \\]\n\nThus:\n\\[ 1 + r \\approx 1.061585 \\]\n\\[ r \\approx 0.061585 \\]\n\nConverting this to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth:\n\\[ r \\approx 6.16\\% \\]\n\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\(\\boxed{6.16}\\).",
