      "full_cot": ", just to , let me compute it using logarithms. 6.07}\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.\n\\boxed{6.07}\n</think>\n\nDr. Fu Manchu has a bank account with an annual interest rate of 6 percent, compounded monthly. We need to find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) that would give the same return if compounded annually.\n\nFirst, we use the compound interest formula for monthly compounding:\n\\[ A = P \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n \\]\nwhere \\( r = 0.06 \\) and \\( n = 12 \\). For one year, this becomes:\n\\[ P \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = P \\left(1 + r_{\\text{annual}}\\right) \\]\n\nThe principal \\( P \\) cancels out, so we have:\n\\[ \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = 1 + r_{\\text{annual}} \\]\n\nCalculating the inside of the left side:\n\\[ 1 + \\frac{0.06}{12} = 1 + 0.005 = 1.005 \\]\n\nWe need to compute \\( (1.005)^{12} \\). Using step-by-step multiplication:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n1.005^1 & = 1.005 \\\\\n1.005^2 & = 1.010025 \\\\\n1.005^3 & \\approx 1.015075125 \\\\\n1.005^4 & \\approx 1.020150501 \\\\\n1.005^5 & \\approx 1.025251002 \\\\\n1.005^6 & \\approx 1.030301502 \\\\\n1.005^7 & \\approx 1.035355506 \\\\\n1.005^8 & \\approx 1.040408016 \\\\\n1.005^9 & \\approx 1.045461025 \\\\\n1.005^{10} & \\approx 1.050525126 \\\\\n1.005^{11} & \\approx 1.055600127 \\\\\n1.005^{12} & \\approx 1.060660127 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThus, \\( (1.005)^{12} \\approx 1.06066 \\). Therefore:\n\\[ 1 + r_{\\text{annual}} = 1.06066 \\]\n\\[ r_{\\text{annual}} = 1.06066 - 1 = 0.06066 \\]\n\nRounding to the nearest hundredth, we get:\n\\[ r \\approx 0.0607 \\]\n\nThus, the equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.",
