      "full_cot": ", let's see. 6.07}.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the equivalent annual interest rate \\( r \\) percent for a bank account that compounds monthly at an annual interest rate of 6 percent, we need to calculate the effective annual rate (EAR).\n\nThe compound interest formula is:\n\\[ A = P \\left(1 + \\frac{r}{n}\\right)^n \\]\n\nFor monthly compounding, we have:\n\\[ A_{\\text{monthly}} = P \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} \\]\n\nFor annual compounding, we have:\n\\[ A_{\\text{annual}} = P (1 + r) \\]\n\nSince the amount after one year should be the same for both compounding methods, we set them equal:\n\\[ \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nCalculating the inside of the left side:\n\\[ 1 + \\frac{0.06}{12} = 1 + 0.005 = 1.005 \\]\n\nThus, the equation becomes:\n\\[ (1.005)^{12} = 1 + r \\]\n\nCalculating \\( (1.005)^{12} \\) step by step:\n\\[ 1.005^{12} \\approx 1.060660127 \\]\n\nTherefore:\n\\[ 1.060660127 = 1 + r \\]\n\\[ r = 1.060660127 - 1 = 0.060660127 \\]\n\nConverting this to a percentage and rounding to the nearest hundredth:\n\\[ r \\approx 6.07\\% \\]\n\nThus, the equivalent annual interest rate is \\boxed{6.07}.",
